)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Status Panel -- Further Fields (?)       !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
}  The ? command, typed alone on the command line, shows further fields
}  of the jobs after JOBNAME; ? again shows the usual ones. Where they do
}  not fit on the screen, the Right key (PF11) moves them, the Left key
}  (PF10) moves them back. NP and JOBNAME stay in place.
}
{  RNUM            }The remote the job came from; blank for local jobs.
{  PROGRAMMER-NAME }The programmer name of the JOB statement.
{  ACCT            }The account number.
{  NOTIFY          }The user told when the job ends.
{  ISYS            }The system that read the job in.
{  RD-TIME RD-DATE }When the job was read in.
{  ESYS            }The system that executes, or executed, the job.
{  ST-TIME ST-DATE }When the job started to execute.
{  CARDS           }The number of input cards.
{  MC              }The message class (MSGCLASS).
{  TOT-LINES       }The number of output lines of the job.
}
}  Times are hh:mm:ss, dates yy.ddd (year and day of the year).
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Status panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHSTO
  &ZUP = ISFHST
)END
